{"name":"French Lime","hex":"#c0ff00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"french","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare food by cutting it into strips.","To kiss (another person) while inserting one’s tongue into the other person's mouth."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/french"},{"term":"lime","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any inorganic material containing calcium, usually calcium oxide (quicklime) or calcium hydroxide (slaked lime).","Any gluey or adhesive substance that traps or captures; sometimes a synonym for birdlime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To treat with calcium hydroxide or calcium oxide (lime).","To smear with birdlime.\n To ensnare, catch, entrap."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lime"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lumia (citrus)","blocks":[{"text":"The lumia is also called the pear lemon, since its shape resembles a pear. It is also called French lime and sometimes sweet lemon, even though it is not necessarily sweet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/71/Castello%2C_collezione_degli_agrumi_02.jpg/330px-Castello%2C_collezione_degli_agrumi_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lumia_(citrus)","wikidata":"Q3840598"},{"title":"Lime (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a color that is a shade of yellow-green, so named because it is a representation of the color of the citrus fruit lime. It is the color that is in between the web color chartreuse and yellow on the color wheel. Alternate names for this color included yellow-green, lemon-lime, lime green, or bitter lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c2/AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg/330px-AosaHGkyuai_%28cropped%29_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(color)","wikidata":"Q906936"},{"title":"Lime (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Lime is a Canadian disco band from Montreal, Quebec. The group was originally composed of married couple Denis and Denyse LePage who had a 1981 number one U.S. Dance hit with \"Your Love\". They continued to perform as recently as 2018, although others have also performed under the name of Lime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Lime_band.jpg/330px-Lime_band.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lime_(band)","wikidata":"Q3241037"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Lumia_-_Limon_%C3%A0_Zucheta_Volkamer_1708_138b.png/500px-Lumia_-_Limon_%C3%A0_Zucheta_Volkamer_1708_138b.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/Lumia_-_Limon_%C3%A0_Zucheta_Volkamer_1708_138b.png/500px-Lumia_-_Limon_%C3%A0_Zucheta_Volkamer_1708_138b.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Lumia by Johann Christoph Volkamer is described as a sweet lemon.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALumia_-_Limon_%C3%A0_Zucheta_Volkamer_1708_138b.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/NHM_-_Citrus_x_limon_3.jpg/500px-NHM_-_Citrus_x_limon_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/NHM_-_Citrus_x_limon_3.jpg/500px-NHM_-_Citrus_x_limon_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Developing fruit","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANHM_-_Citrus_x_limon_3.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/3_etrog.JPG/330px-3_etrog.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/3_etrog.JPG/330px